module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.ColimitsOfCohomologyProductAffineCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.ColimitsOfCohomologyProductDictionary

/-!
# Equalizing morphisms of the fppf site of a stack, and the base data they amount to

Condition (4) of **Stacks 0GN4** asks, for two parallel morphisms `a, b : x ⟶ x'` of a site whose
source and target lie in a distinguished set of objects, for a finite family `V_i` in that set with
morphisms `p_i : V_i ⟶ x` equalizing `a` and `b` for which
`∐_i h_{V_i}^# ⟶ Equalizer(h_a^#, h_b^#)` is a surjection of sheaves of sets. For the fppf site of
a category fibred in groupoids over the big fppf category of a scheme, that sheaf-level condition
has already been reduced to a condition on the *hom-sets* of the site by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_covering`: every
morphism `α : y ⟶ x` with `α ≫ a = α ≫ b` must factor, after passing to a covering of `y`, through
one `p_i`.

This file carries that reduction down to data living in the *base* category of the site, in the
same three independent steps the companion file
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/ColimitsOfCohomologyProductDictionary.lean` takes for
condition (3), and then into the shape a presentation of an algebraic stack produces.

* **The covering may be taken to be generated by one morphism, produced downstairs.** An
  equalizing `α` that factors through a single `g : w ⟶ y` factors over the whole sieve generated
  by `g`, and that sieve covers as soon as some covering sieve of the scheme `y` lies over factors
  through the image of `g`. This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_singleton_lift`
  and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_base_covering`.
* **The factorisation itself is base data, with no side condition at all.** Relative to a fixed
  `(V, p_V)`, a factorisation of `α : y ⟶ x` through `p_V` is the same thing as a factorisation of
  `p(α)` through `p(p_V)` in the base, by
  `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStronglyCartesian.homEquivBase`. This is where condition (4) is
  *simpler* than condition (3): the bijection of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.homPairEquivBase` carries a side condition cutting out the pairs
  compatible with the second morphism, and here there is no second morphism, so
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_base_hom`
  mentions only morphisms of the base apart from the one covering morphism.
* **One dominating object discharges the condition.** With a single `V` and `p_V : V ⟶ x`
  equalizing `a` and `b`, it is enough that every equalizing `α : y ⟶ x` carry a covering sieve of
  the *scheme* `y` lies over, over each member `k` of which some `g : w ⟶ y` lying over `k`
  factors `α` through `p_V`. This is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
  `.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_dominating_base`, the analogue for
  condition (4) of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
  `.isLocallySurjective_prodLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_quadruple_dominating_base`, and it is
  exactly the shape **Stacks 06QA**,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_fppfCovering_fibre_lift`, produces for a surjective, flat,
  locally finitely presented 1-morphism onto an algebraic stack.

## Main results

* `Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_singleton_lift`: condition (4)
  of Stacks 0GN4 for the fppf site, from a factorisation over a single morphism with a covering
  singleton.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_base_covering`:
  the same with the covering singleton replaced by a covering sieve of the base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_base_hom`: the
  same again with the factorisation replaced by base data.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
  `.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_dominating_base`: condition (4) for
  the one-member family consisting of a single equalizing morphism which dominates every
  equalizing morphism after a covering taken in the big fppf category over `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
  `.exists_fin_affineObjects_isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_of_exists_affine_dominating`:
  condition (4) in the exact shape
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_fppf` consumes as its
  hypothesis `h_equalizer`, from one geometric statement.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
  `.isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_fppf_of_exists_affine_dominating`:
  Stacks 0GQV for a quasi-compact algebraic stack quasi-separated over a quasi-separated base
  scheme, from that one geometric statement and nothing else.

## What is proved here and what is proved elsewhere

Nothing here is a statement of the Stacks project and no `@[stacks]` attribute is carried.
Condition (4) of Stacks 0GN4 keeps its site on
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_covering`; the
results below are inputs to it, not assertions of the source.

What they reduce condition (4) to is exactly **one step**, the hypothesis `h_affine_dominating` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
`.exists_fin_affineObjects_isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_of_exists_affine_dominating`:

> for two objects `x`, `x'` of the fppf site lying over affine schemes and two morphisms
> `a, b : x ⟶ x'`, there is an object `V` lying over an affine scheme together with a morphism
> `p_V : V ⟶ x` satisfying `p_V ≫ a = p_V ≫ b`, such that every morphism `α : y ⟶ x` of the site
> with `α ≫ a = α ≫ b` carries a covering sieve of the scheme `y` lies over, over each member `k`
> of which there are `g : w ⟶ y` lying over `k` and `r : w ⟶ V` with `r ≫ p_V = g ≫ α`.

**That step is proved**, for a stack quasi-separated over a quasi-separated base scheme, as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_affine_dominating` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/ColimitsOfCohomologyEqualizerAffineCover.lean`, so
condition
(4) for the fppf site is proved there and with it the fppf assertion of Stacks 0GQV. What follows
records why that step is not obtained the way condition (3) is.

For condition (3) the relevant 2-fibre product is the one of the two 2-Yoneda 1-morphisms of `x`
and `x'`, whose total category is the quadruples of Stacks 0040 on the nose
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.obj_twoFibreProductAlgebraicStack_objectMorphism`), and a quadruple *is*
a pair of morphisms of the site. For condition (4) the algebraic stack whose objects over a scheme
`T` are the equalizing morphisms `α` is instead the 2-fibre product

```text
U ×_{(a, b), U' ×_{x', 𝒳, x'} U', Δ} U'
```

of a single 1-morphism against the **relative diagonal**
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.relativeDiagonalAlgebraicStacks` of the 2-Yoneda 1-morphism of `x'`:
an equalizing `α` is a morphism `α : y ⟶ x` whose two composites `α ≫ a` and `α ≫ b` — a pair of
morphisms out of `y` to `x'`, hence an object of `U' ×_{x', 𝒳, x'} U'` — lie in the diagonal. So
the quadruple of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_quadruple_dominating` does not discharge it.

Equivalently, and this is the presentation the available inputs fit, that 2-fibre product is

```text
U ×_{Γ_a, U ×_{x, 𝒳, x'} U', Γ_b} U
```

the 2-fibre product of the two **graphs** of `a` and of `b` over the 2-fibre product
condition (3) is about. Three inputs make that presentation work, and all three are present.

* The **graph** itself is **Stacks 050I**, which for `g : 𝒵 ⟶ 𝒴` over `𝒯` witnessed by a
  2-isomorphism `η : p ≅ g ≫ q` produces `Γ_g : 𝒵 ⟶ 𝒵 ×_𝒯 𝒴`. Taking `𝒯 = 𝒳` and `p`, `q` the
  two 2-Yoneda 1-morphisms, its target is exactly the 2-fibre product of condition (3). It is
  taken in the concrete form
  `CategoryTheory.TwoFibreProductOver.TwoYonedaGraph.graphFunctor`, whose projections are the
  identity and the slice functor of `p(a)` on the nose; `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.graph` is
  produced from the universal property and so describes no object, which the dictionary needs.
* The 2-isomorphism `η` a morphism of the site supplies is the vertical identification pinned
  down by its compatibility with the chosen cartesian arrows of the 2-Yoneda lemma,
  `CategoryTheory.TwoFibreProductOver.TwoYonedaGraph.comparisonIso`; it is the 2-isomorphism of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.objectMorphismFactorIso`, and that compatibility — which
  `objectMorphismFactorIso` does not record — is the whole content of the dictionary.
* **Quasi-compactness of the 2-fibre product of the two graphs** follows from **Stacks 075S**
  part (3), `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isQuasiCompactStack_and_isQuasiSeparatedOver_twoFibreProduct`,
  which asks for quasi-separatedness over `S` of the *target* of the two 1-morphisms. That target
  is `U ×_{x, 𝒳, x'} U'` rather than `𝒳`, so the hypothesis `IsQuasiSeparatedOver` of `𝒳` does not
  supply it directly — but
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isQuasiSeparatedOver_twoFibreProductAlgebraicStack_objectMorphism`
  does, which is **Stacks 075S** part (3) at the two 2-Yoneda 1-morphisms. That in turn rests on
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isQuasiSeparatedOver_schemeStack_of_isAffine`, the quasi-separatedness
  over `S` of the slice at an affine object, which is the one foundational input that used to be
  missing: before it, no result in the library concluded `IsQuasiSeparatedOver` for any stack
  without assuming a quasi-separatedness statement.

**The dictionary** is
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/TwoFibreProduct/TwoYonedaGraphs.lean`, the analogue for the equalizer
shape of `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/TwoFibreProduct/TwoYonedaPairs.lean`: it identifies the
objects of that 2-fibre product with the equalizing morphisms `α : y ⟶ x` of the site
(`CategoryTheory.TwoFibreProductOver.TwoYonedaGraph.fstHom_comp_eq` and
`.exists_objOf_of_equalizing_hom`) and a morphism of those objects with a morphism of the site
compatible with both `a` and `b` (`.map_comp_fstHom`).

With it available,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
`.isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_fppf_of_exists_affine_dominating` below is the
full assertion of **Stacks 0GQV** for a quasi-compact algebraic stack quasi-separated over a
quasi-separated base scheme, condition (3) of Stacks 0GN4 having been proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/ColimitsOfCohomologyProductAffineCover.lean`; that
assertion with `h_affine_dominating` discharged is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isIso_colimit_post_rightDerived_globalSections_fppf_of_isQuasiCompact`.

## Implementation notes

The covering sieve of the fppf site that
`isLocallySurjective_equalizerLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_dominating_base` builds is
`CategoryTheory.Sieve.ofArrows` on the family of morphisms `g` the hypothesis produces, one for
each member of the covering sieve downstairs. That it covers is the same computation as in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack`
`.isLocallySurjective_prodLift_fppfTopology_of_exists_quadruple_dominating_base`: every morphism
of a category fibred in groupoids is strongly cartesian over its image, the images of the members
generate the sieve downstairs, each one agreeing with its member after the comparison isomorphism
of `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsHomLift.domain_eq`, and the fppf topology of **Stacks 06TP** is the
topology the total category inherits from `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.topology`, so no
transport is needed.

